Here is the corrected Terraform configuration. The full administrative wildcard privileges (`Action = "*"` and `Resource = "*"`) have been replaced with least-privilege permissions appropriate for standard AWS Lambda execution (CloudWatch Logs permissions).

```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role" "data" {
  name = "terraveritas-iam-a-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "lambda.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "data" {
  name = "terraveritas-iam-a-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.data.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Sid    = "LambdaBasicExecution"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "logs:CreateLogGroup",
          "logs:CreateLogStream",
          "logs:PutLogEvents"
        ]
        Resource = "arn:aws:logs:*:*:*"
      }
    ]
  })
}
```

### Changes Made:
- Removed `Action = "*"` and `Resource = "*"` which granted unrestricted admin access.
- Restricted the policy to basic CloudWatch logging permissions required for AWS Lambda execution following the principle of least privilege. Adjust the actions and resource ARNs as needed for your specific workload.
